WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A rubber hand on a table can sometimes feel like part of someone's body.
That's what researchers reported in 1998.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Their experiment paired what people saw with what they felt.
The reported effect is real evidence worth studying.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
But later research raised a harder question:
do expectations and the wording of questions help shape those reports?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
That debate matters. A strange experience
is not the same thing as a proven explanation.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And no rubber-hand experiment establishes what a meditation audio program
can do. They test different things.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Before you buy Zen12, check its format, the actual terms, the evidence,
and whether a free routine already meets your needs.
